WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.150
Within the surprising world,
the uncertainties are becoming higher and

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.250
higher due to potential risks,

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.040
changes in trade as well as
the changing technologies.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.800
And the uncertainties
provide opportunities.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.630
This program is not about just
how to do procurement, logistics.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:25.160
But we try to link how product
development, design thinking,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.080
customer service, channel managements,
are all integrated.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.240
Because this is the new way.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.360
Innovation is the centerpiece
of our focus.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.930
You need to innovate the way you work.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.130
Where you locate your factories?

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.070
How do you do outsourcing, offshoring?

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.450
Reassuring.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.620
Self driving cars, robots, 3D printing,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.450
you can recreate a new
form of a supply chain.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:59.270
&gt;&gt; This program gives you
a complete supply chain view.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:03.110
All the way from defining
the strategy to your execution.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:09.090
So it gives you the full visibility on
how you can improve your supply chain.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:16.930
&gt;&gt; Supply chain today has evolved
into becoming a weapon for attack.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.790
It is a value creating strategy to
gain market share in new markets.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.860
Increase revenues to improve margins.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.040
&gt;&gt; We were given the tools to meet
the challenges that we are facing today.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.484
&gt;&gt; The business cases
are absolutely fantastic.

00:01:31.484 --> 00:01:35.980
&gt;&gt; You need to strengthen your partners,
you need to strengthen your supply bases,

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.560
you need to strengthen your
customer relationships so

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.150
that it's holistic involving
every member of the supply chain.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.170
&gt;&gt; I can only remain in business
if I bring value to my customers,

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.860
because it's all about value.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.990
&gt;&gt; If I go to my customers, I'm able to
show them what I am doing differently.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:59.780
&gt;&gt; A good football team must have
good defense, and also good offense,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.500
and we are helping our executives
to build a foundation of defense,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.090
but also have really
strong offense as well.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:09.830
&gt;&gt; I'm very,

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:14.810
very impressed by the passion of the
people that are teaching these classes.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:19.279
&gt;&gt; I would recommend this schools to
anybody who wants to make their supply

00:02:19.279 --> 00:02:20.778
chain more strategic.

00:02:20.778 --> 00:02:23.913
&gt;&gt; We want our target
executives to think big.

00:02:23.913 --> 00:02:26.940
Willing to leverage innovations.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.900
&gt;&gt; This is a course that I'll
definitely recommend to others.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.230
&gt;&gt; I believe that to be the best,
you have to learn from the best.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:38.024
&gt;&gt; I truly believe that this is the best
supply chain programs in the world.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:42.179
[MUSIC]

